=== layout: section

# Grading and Assessment

=== layout: one-panel

# Assignments, Quizzes, and Exams

@body

- Assignments\: Tasks completed outside of class
  - Aims to reinforce learning or explore new topics.
  - Assigned weekly, 5-15 points, Unlimited retakes allowed.
  - Collaboration and seeking help encouraged.
- Quizzes\: Short assessments to test knowledge on recent topics.
  - Aims to quickly assess understanding of recent material.
  - 20 points, 30 min, individual.
  - Followed by a group quiz during class.
- Exams\: Cumulative assessments covering course material.
  - Cumulative, mid-term/final.
  - 100 points total (50 points/75 minutes each part).
  - Completed individually.

=== layout: two-panels

# Graded vs Total Percentage

@left

- Graded percentage only includes items that have a grade
- Ignores all uncompleted assignments
- More accurate when Dr. Voss has ungraded entries in the grade book

@right

- Total percentage is all gradable items in blackboard.
- Gives you a zero score on all uncompleted assignments.
  - including assignments waiting for a grade from the professor.
- More accurate when you have unattempted blackboard assignments

=== layout: section

# Quiz/Exam

=== layout: one-panel

# Don’t Panic

@body

- If you experience internet troubles or non-academic distractions during a quiz/exam\:
  - 1. Don’t panic
  - 2. Stop and close the quiz/exam without looking at all the questions
  - 3. Contact me immediately, preferably via Discord, but you do not need to rush
- Note\: Once class begins, I no longer check my email.
- If you haven't looked at all the questions, I can reset the quiz/exam
- If you have looked at some questions, I can create a new custom quiz/exam with only the portion that you haven't seen yet.

=== layout: one-panel

# Illness Policy

@body

- Since COVID, I am trying to be more considerate of student illnesses.
- If you are sick, let me know. I will provide an extension.
- If a major event interferes (car accident, etc.), again contact me.
- Communication is always helpful.

